{"chunk_id": "ee0ff8602050", "text": "This section recounts precedents for preserving royal lineages through unconventional means and sets up the birth of key figures in the Bharata dynasty. A blind sage abandoned by greedy sons is rescued by King Vali, who asks the rishi to produce heirs. Through a series of events involving the queen\u2019s refusal and later compliance, the sage fathers sons whose names become those of major eastern kingdoms\u2014Anga, Vanga, Kalinga, Pundra, and Suhma\u2014illustrating how Brahmin seed could continue Kshatriya lines. Bhishma cites this example to advise Satyavati on preserving the Bharata lineage after Vichitravirya\u2019s death. Satyavati then reveals her secret past with the sage Parashara and the miraculous birth of their son Vyasa, who divided the Vedas. She proposes summoning Vyasa to father heirs, establishing the crucial mechanism that will lead to the next generation of the Kuru dynasty.\nBhishma recounts precedent for Brahmin-sired heirs and Satyavati reveals Vyasa\u2019s birth, proposing him to father heirs on Vichitravirya\u2019s widows.\nThemes: dynastic succession, niyoga tradition, origin of Vyasa, royal lineage, dharma and duty", "vector": [0.016723092645406723, -0.01847764663398266, -0.004389811772853136, -0.005887350998818874, -0.008505473844707012, 0.024563755840063095, -0.005291076842695475, -0.004544020630419254, -0.021383626386523247, -0.02788095921278, 0.00017059352830983698, -0.0014846884878352284, 0.00670637097209692, 0.01193919125944376, -0.023412328213453293, 0.008142226375639439, 0.03758583590388298, 0.0010254888329654932, 0.031170746311545372, -0.008683671243488789, -0.009444435127079487, -0.0036359017249196768, 0.0008374396711587906, 0.018710672855377197, -0.01477663405239582, 0.020711960271000862, 0.017655199393630028, -0.008820746093988419, 0.005585786886513233, -0.011445722542703152, -0.007436293177306652, 0.0058633629232645035, -0.002164063975214958, -0.009643192403018475, -0.02630460076034069, -0